WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.834 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Welcome back.

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much
for having me.

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.870
-First of all, congratulations.
You have a baby on the way.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, yes, yes.
-Very exciting.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.542 line:92%
Yes. Procreation is under way.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is under way.
-Yeah.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.145 line:92%
-And you were actually --

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:14.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
You presented at the Tonys
on Sunday night.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did. I did.
-And how was that?

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:19.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
How was that experience?
-You know, it was -- it was --

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:24.324
It was fun until I had to do
the actual job of presenting.

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:27.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I was --
I was sat backstage.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:29.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they called me.
And I stood up.

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:32.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went to go
and do my little spiel,

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:33.800 line:92%
read the monitor and stuff,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this happens to me
sometimes.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:36.369 line:92%
Like, I'm still pretty active

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:38.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I take my SoulCycle class
and everything.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:42.575
But occasionally, I'll stand up
and get profoundly winded.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:43.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And this was one of
those occasions.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:50.717
And I was like, "Oh, my God.
I don't have access to oxygen."

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:51.618 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:52.185 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Like, at all.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:56.356
And I'm supposed to be reading
in front of thousands of people.

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:57.590 line:92%
In fact, millions of people."

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:02.128
So, yeah, I eventually, like,
recovered and found my breath.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.530 line:92%
But I couldn't stop and say,

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:06.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Sorry, guys,
I'm just really pregnant now."

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:06.800 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn't want to detract
from the nominees, you know?

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:10.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
It wasn't about me
being pregnant in that second.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:13.406 size:84% position:42%
-Well, it's interesting
because I was watching.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I did not put
the two together.

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:16.242 line:92%
-Well, thank you for that.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I had a moment,
though of --

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:20.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My husband did. He was there.
And he was concerned.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
"'Cause I've seen that
happen to you

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:24.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
sometimes when you go up
and down our stairs."

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:25.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, but --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:26.119 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I wasn't concerned.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:29.956
I just thought, "Wow, Claire is
so excited about this award."

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.024 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
"She's so..."
-Well, I was.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:33.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But, you know, hopefully

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:37.097
excitement translates, you know,
in a slightly different way.

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:40.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you think that
your shortness of breath then

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.367 line:92%
was exacerbated by the fact that

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
you then had to
speak on television?

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.672
-Maybe they had something to do
with each other.

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:48.007 size:81% position:41%
But, like, I've spoken
on television before.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:50.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, sure.
-Like, for a few years now.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:51.344 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So I think pregnancy
was the thing.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.414 line:92%
-That was the main thing? Yeah.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:56.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But, yeah, so, anyway.
-Anyway.

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:57.183 line:92%
-There are humbling moments.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:59.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I also think that would
be a nice thing

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:01.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
to tie back for your child
years from now,

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:04.124
that you could show them exactly
what they did to you.

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:05.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What this person has cost me.
-Yeah.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah. The list is long.
-Yeah.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:08.862 line:92%
-Already. Not been born yet.

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:11.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But just for you to be able
to be like,

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:15.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Don't make me show you
the Tonys again!"

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:15.969 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:16.970 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Go to your room!"

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have a 5-year-old.
-I do.

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:22.475
-What is his reaction so far to
the idea of an oncoming sibling?

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:24.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's pretty --
I think he's keen.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
he's mostly enthusiastic.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:29.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, when we first told him
I was pregnant,

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
he said,
"That took a long time, Mom."

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:32.352 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:33.887 line:92%
"That took a lot of days."

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:38.291
And I was like, "Okay.
Yeah, we've been working on it."

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
But -- So, yeah, so I guess
he was into it.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then there was, like,
a little wobble.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.396 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And then he was worried

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:45.231 size:88% position:44%
that I was going to love
the baby more than him.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:48.201
And then anybody who walked
through the door, I was --

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.169 line:92%
I loved more than him, you know.

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:51.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he seems to have gotten
through that, too.

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:52.539 line:92%
And now he hugs my belly.

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:54.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's really great.
-And it's sweet.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think it's going to go
up and down.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:57.243 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:58.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How's your baby
with number two?

00:02:58.444 --> 00:02:59.412 line:92%
-Well, it's a difference in age.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:02.081
Yours is five now.
-Five, yeah. He's like a person.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:02.849 line:92%
-The 2-year-old doesn't --

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:06.953
you know, I don't think he quite
understands jealousy yet.

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:08.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-As an emotion.

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:10.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think it's coming.
-Yeah.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.525 line:92%
-But mostly, he just thinks --

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
he treats the 2-month-old
like a joke.

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:19.132
Every time you say, "Look, it's
your baby," he's like...

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:19.666 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:20.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I mean it kind of is.
-Yeah.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're useless
for a really long time.

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:24.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And the second one
is really useless.

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:25.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really useless. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:28.474
-Because the first one, at
least, is interesting in the way

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
like watching "Planet Earth"
is interesting.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:31.711 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Right, right, right.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.646
-You're like, "Oh, wow, they do
this and they do that."

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:36.549
But now you're like, "I don't
want to watch that episode of

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:39.319 size:88% position:44%
'Planet Earth' again."
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:39.852 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So he's great,
but you kind of are --

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:43.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
I still feel like
it's a preview to a movie

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:44.791 line:92%
I eventually will want to see.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. Okay.
-Yeah.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:49.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I'm prepared.
-Yeah, good.

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:51.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, this movie is
adapted from a play

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:55.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I saw back in New York
when it was here.

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:57.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's about parents
trying to get,

00:03:57.737 --> 00:04:01.574
for those who couldn't tell from
the clip, their kid into school.

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:02.775 line:92%
Tell us a little more about it.

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:05.612
-Yeah, I mean, it's parents are
trying to get

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
their 4 1/2-year-old kid
into school.

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:10.617
This 4 1/2-year-old kid happens
to love wearing dresses

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:13.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
and is sort of obsessed with
all things princess.

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:16.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's becoming clear that
maybe he's not conforming

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.524 line:92%
to these strict gender norms.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.959 line:92%
He's gender fluid, expansive.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:21.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
The language is intense
right now.

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:24.964
But yeah, so, and so they have
a friend who is an educator,

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:28.034
and as they're applying to
schools, suggests that maybe

00:04:28.034 --> 00:04:30.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
they make more of this fact
rather than less.

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:32.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
And suddenly they're just
thinking of him

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:35.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
in these different terms
and they're -- I don't know.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:36.943 line:92%
They become kind of anxious

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:39.379 size:78% position:39%
that he's going to be
labeled by society.

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:41.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's really called
"A Kid like Jake"

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:43.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the emphasis isn't so much
on the kid.

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:46.519 size:84% position:42%
It's really the parents
and just this crisis

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they're kind of --
they spiral into.

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:51.924
But ultimately, I mean, it's
really just kind of a portrait

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:52.759 line:92%
of a marriage and a family.

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:55.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's about parents just
trying to figure out

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:57.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
the best way to understand
who their child is

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.799
and help them navigate their way
through the world.

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:01.768 size:84% position:42%
So I think in some ways
it's really specific

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:05.505
and it's this very topical idea
of gender identity and politics.

00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:09.208
But it's also just about, you
know, releasing your children

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:13.212
into the world and trusting that
they're going to be fine.

